1.    (Currently Amended) A wearable fetal health monitoring device for determining a health [[heath]] condition of a fetus based on biosignals of an expecting mother and the fetus, the wearable fetal health monitoring device comprising:a passive sensor configured to provide mechano-acoustically sensed phonocardiogram (aPCG) data from a first location on a maternal torso a- microelectromechanical system (MEMS) accelerometer that converts an acoustic wave sensed in an abdominal region into an abdominal acoustic signal;

an optical sensor a pulse oximeter that generates a configured to provide optically sensed maternal photoplethysmogram (mPPG) data [[value]] from a second location on the maternal torso a pulse sensed in the abdominal region;

a securing device configured to provide skin contact of the passive sensor and the optical sensor to the maternal torso for continuous non-invasive non-clinical monitoring;

a ferroelectric nanogenerator sensor that detects abdominal pressure waves; and

a microcontroller configured for [[to]]:generate a maternal phonocardiogram (mPCG) value from the abdominal acoustic signal;

calculate a first maternal heart rate (mHR) value from the mPCG value;

calculate a second mHR value from the mPPG value;

compare the first mHR value with the second mHR value to identify a noise correction value; and

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.432.067monitoring fetal movement (fM) using the passive sensor while operating in a first mode, wherein the first mode is a reduced power mode; and

upon detecting reduced fM activity, transitioning to a second mode comprising:decomposing the mechano-acoustically sensed aPCG data using the optically sensed mPPG data apply the identified noise correction value to the mPCG value to extract [[a]] mechano-acoustically sensed fetal phonocardiogram (fPCG) data [[value]];

determining fetal heart rate variability (fHRV) data from the mechano- acoustically sensed fPCG data; and providing an alert to the expecting mother based on the fHRV data.



2.    (Canceled)



3.    (Canceled) The device of claim 1, wherein the microcontroller is further configured to calculate from the fPCG value at least one of: a fetal heart rate (fHR) value and a fetal heart rate variability (fHRV) value.



4.    (Currently Amended) The wearable fetal health monitoring device of claim 1, wherein the microcontroller is further configured to calculate [[a]] fetal movement (fM)data [[value]] from the mechano-acoustically sensed aPCG data abdominal acoustic signal.



5.    (Currently Amended) The wearable fetal health monitoring device of claim 1, wherein:the optical sensor pulse oximeter is further configured to sense [[a]] maternal peripheral capillary oxygen saturation (mSpO2) data [[value]], and

transitioning to the second mode is further based upon detecting reduced mSpO2 data.

