determining fetal heart rate variability (fHRV) data from the mechano-acoustically sensed fPCG data; and providing an alert to the expecting mother based on the fHRV data.



22.   (New) The wearable fetal health monitoring device of claim 1, wherein determining fHRV data from the mechano-acoustically sensed fPCG data comprises using a Hidden Semi-Markov Model (HSMM).



23.   (New) The wearable fetal health monitoring device of claim 1, wherein determining fHRV data from the mechano-acoustically sensed fPCG data comprises using empirical mode decomposition (EMD).



24.   (New) The wearable fetal health monitoring device of claim 1, wherein the passive sensor is selected from the group consisting of a microelectromechanical system (MEMS), an accelerometer, and a ferroelectric nanogenerator sensor.



25.   (New) The wearable fetal health monitoring device of claim 1, wherein the securing device is selected from the group consisting of a belt, a band, and an adhesive patch.
